# M1 Infrastructure Legacy Git Sync — Manual Service Failure

Date: 2026-08-26
Scope: M1 preflight infrastructure unblocker
Status: activation stopped; diagnosis pending

## Passed gates before the failure

- Installed scripts matched the committed Control-source SHA-256 values.
- Installed scripts are owned by `root:root` with mode `0755`.
- Shell syntax check passed.
- `systemd-analyze verify` passed for all six planned units.
- The manual MommyRamona HTTP health-check service completed successfully.

## Error

The first manual start of `tu1nz-legacy-git-sync.service` failed because its
control process exited with a non-zero status.

## Impact and containment

- The new health and Git-sync timers remain disabled.
- The recurring encrypted-backup timer has not been enabled.
- The `chatops` crontab has not been changed.
- M1 application implementation remains untouched.

## Cause

Not yet established. No corrective change is authorized until the service
status and journal have been read and the exact failure has been identified.

## Next diagnostic action

Use the versioned gate's read-only `gitlog` action to capture the full service
status and the latest 120 journal lines. Based on that evidence, document a
specific repair and rollback plan before retrying the service.
